            <ArticleTitle>[Feves and left upper-quadrant abdominal pain in a Tunisian child. Amebic abcess of the spleen].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>29-31</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Amebiasis is a rarely localized in the spleen, and its preoperative diagnosis is difficult. We report the case of an 11-year-old Tunisian girl who presented with fever and left upper-quadrant abdominal pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
